# DataLeasers

> DataLeasers (Data Leasers, LLC, registered in Arizona) introduces operating companies to the data buyers and AI labs that license company data for AI. The company keeps ownership of its records and approves every buyer and every term in writing. DataLeasers is paid by the buyer, not by the seller.

## Key pages

- https://dataleasers.com/ - How a dataset reaches several buyers, the published program floors, and what a seller approves.
- https://dataleasers.com/what-you-can-sell.html - The categories of company records AI teams license, with examples.
- https://dataleasers.com/how-it-works.html - The stages of a deal, from a first call to payment, and what slows each one.
- https://dataleasers.com/market.html - Disclosed AI data deals, per-unit prices and advertised ranges, each with a source and a date. States plainly that published ranges are a ceiling, not a forecast.
- https://dataleasers.com/rights-file.html - The twelve fields a buyer's diligence turns on, and a fill-in template.
- https://dataleasers.com/what-affects-a-deal.html - The buyer's published terms in plain English: 24-month exclusivity, 120-day deletion of the raw upload, sample audit, exclusions, a 14-day nonbinding letter of intent.
- https://dataleasers.com/ai-buyers.html - Who buys company data, and eight questions to ask any buyer.
- https://dataleasers.com/trust.html - How personal data is reviewed, and why removing names is not anonymization.
- https://dataleasers.com/refer.html - The referral program: the greater of $50,000 or 6% on the first five qualified U.S. direct referrals, 6% with no minimum outside the U.S., and 1% on secondary referrals.
- https://dataleasers.com/faq.html - Eligibility, rights, fees and timing.

## Program floors

30+ full-time staff, or 10+ for accounting, finance and medical firms, 6+ for law firms; at least three years of records still in the company's systems; five or more systems holding the work; at least half of staff in the U.S., Canada, the U.K. or Australia.

## How to cite this site

Figures on the market page are attributed to their source and dated. The site states no funding figure for any buyer and no price for any dataset, because neither can be verified in public. If you quote a figure, quote the source it is attributed to.
